Title: Nick and Me
Credit: Written by
Author: Author
Source: Adapted from book
Draft date: 7/30/2026

FADE IN:

INT. KIRK STREET APARTMENT - DAY

Action: A modest fifth-floor apartment on Kirk Street in Milwaukee. The faded wallpaper and scuffed floors tell stories of hard times. NARRATOR, a lean young man with hesitant eyes, stands in the small living room. MA, a tired woman with brown hair, sits at a worn kitchen table fumbling with a pill bottle.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Big brother was mine. Not that stupid book about a weird, all-seeing world—but the real deal. Nick was the guy everybody feared. With a pair of arms like steel wrecking balls and a face held together by the remnants of old fights, he became both protector and tyrant after Dad left.

Action: Flash images of NICK hauling heavy grocery bags up a narrow stairwell, his scars visible, his reddish-brown hair unkempt. The memory of a gym brawl at Moxie’s flickers in the corners.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
I still remember how even at Moxie’s gym, when a guy dropped his 40-pound bar at the sight of Nick, everyone knew who ruled these streets.

MA 
(murmuring to herself)
Where did I put my pain pills…?

NARRATOR (V.O.)
And through it all, Ma and I held on—one ragged family in a relentless world.

  
INT. JOE'S BAR - NIGHT

Action: A dimly lit bar filled with the hum of a televised Packers game and the clink of glasses. NARRATOR sits at the counter nursing a beer, trying to escape the weight of home.

Action: The door swings open with a heavy thud. NICK, broad-shouldered and scarred, strides in. His presence fills the room as patrons subtly part.

NICK
Hey, little brother. What’s shakin’?

NARRATOR
(nervously)
I don’t know. Nothin’.

NICK
(angry, low)
What’s the matter? I can tell you’re hidin’ something. Ma’s been actin’ up again. Missing her doctor’s visit—now we’re two weeks behind. You gotta watch her, man!

NARRATOR
I’m sorry. I was with someone.

NICK
(voice rising)
With someone? Really? You think a girl is worth leaving Ma in this mess?

Action: Nick slaps NARRATOR on the back and glares, then storms out, leaving an uneasy silence amid the clatter and game noise.

  
INT. MILWAUKEE LIBRARY - EVENING

Action: Warm, aged light floods an old Milwaukee library with wooden shelves and large, timeworn windows. NARRATOR wanders cautiously among the stacks.

LIBRARIAN
(softly)
Do you have a library card?

NARRATOR
No. How do I get one?

Action: The LIBRARIAN, a kindly older woman, prints a temporary paper card and slides it across the counter.

LIBRARIAN
Just write your name and address. A plastic card will come in the mail soon.

Action: NARRATOR scribbles his details on the paper and then drifts toward the classics section. His fingers hover over a worn copy of “Wuthering Heights” as his eyes light up with curiosity.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
In those pages, I found a world that made me feel seen—a stark contrast to my own rough existence.

  
INT. JAVA HUT - NIGHT

Action: A trendy coffee shop with warm lighting and quiet jazz music. The décor hints at academia and youthful ambition. At a small table near a back wall sits SIONNA, a woman with short brown hair, light blue eyes, and a necklace bearing a fish symbol. She exudes quiet confidence.

NARRATOR 
(approaching, a bit hesitant)
Hi. Sionna? This is the guy that got your number outside the pizzeria. Do you remember me?

SIONNA
(smiling, assured)
Of course I do. How are you doing?

NARRATOR
I’m fine. I was wondering if you—if you’d like that cup of coffee?

SIONNA
Absolutely.

Action: They sit down. The ambience softens as their conversation drifts to literature.

SIONNA
(leaning in)
What are you reading right now?

NARRATOR
Wuthering Heights. It’s about a love so destructive and profound… like a force of nature.

SIONNA
(chuckling)
I know it well. Everything changes—just as that tree becomes a chair and eventually returns to the earth. Life, love… it’s all in flux.

Action: Their words blend with the soft clatter of cups, each glance deepening an unspoken connection.

  
INT. KIRK STREET APARTMENT - EVENING

Action: The apartment feels heavier now. MA sits in silence as NARRATOR enters. In the living room, tension crackles. NICK paces, his anger evident in every clenched fist and reddened face.

NICK
(firm, furious)
Ma missed her doctor’s appointment yesterday, you ass! Where the hell were you?

NARRATOR
(quietly, remorseful)
I'm sorry, Nick. I was with someone...

NICK
(voice rising)
With someone? Think about your priorities, little brother! Ma deserves someone who’s here—who’s responsible!

Action: Nick whirls sharply and storms out, slamming the front door. NARRATOR stands frozen, torn between regret and the weight of responsibilities.

Action: The unresolved tension lingers in the silent halls, setting the stage for what’s to come.

  
INT. DOCTOR'S OFFICE - AFTERNOON

Action: NARRATOR sits in a chair by a window, the subdued light revealing his tired eyes. DR. CARSON, calm yet urgent, stands beside a clipboard.

DR. CARSON
Your mother's blood pressure is dangerously high. We need to take her for emergency observation. I’ll admit her immediately and start her on IV medication.

NARRATOR
(uneasy)
But she’s been taking her pills… I don’t understand.

Action: NARRATOR fumbles with his phone and dials. The phone rings and NICK’s voice explodes through the speaker.

NICK
(angry, over phone)
What the hell is this all about now?

NARRATOR
(on the phone, defensive)
Ma’s confused and in pain. The doctor says—she’s at risk of a stroke. I’m taking her to the hospital.

DR. CARSON
(quietly, to NARRATOR)
Please, make sure she gets here promptly.

Action: NARRATOR hangs up, his face heavy with worry as DR. CARSON scribbles notes.

  
EXT. HOSPITAL PARKING LOT - AFTERNOON

Action: NARRATOR, accompanied by MA in a wheelchair, stands beside a waiting car. The grey sky and distant siren echo urgency. NICK arrives, his fury barely contained, stepping into the lot.

NICK
(frustrated)
What the hell is this all about? You can’t be serious.

NARRATOR
(resigned)
Dr. Carson insists. Ma’s condition isn’t normal, and we can’t risk her getting worse.

Action: With a silent nod from NICK, they help Ma into the car. The vehicle speeds off into the uncertain afternoon light.

  
EXT. HOSPITAL ENTRANCE - DAY

Action: A few days later, NARRATOR exits the hospital into a mild, sunlit day. SIONNA waits near the entrance; her eyes, light blue like shining diamonds, soften at the sight of him. They exchange tentative smiles and step aside to talk.

SIONNA
(softly)
Sometimes stepping out of those walls does wonders for the heart and mind.

NARRATOR
(thoughtful)
I’ve been reading about Buddhism... about attachment and finding peace within ourselves.

SIONNA
(chuckling gently)
You always had a way with words. Just remember: you already find that peace at the end of every yoga class.

Action: They begin to walk along the sidewalk, the conversation weaving through gentle philosophy and unspoken hope.

  
INT. HOSPITAL ROOM - NIGHT

Action: In a quiet hospital room dimly lit by moonlight filtering through blinds, NARRATOR sits in a chair beside MA’s bed. Her gentle snores and the rhythmic beep of machines create a lulling backdrop.

Action: NARRATOR drifts into a troubled sleep. In his dream, chaos surrounds him—a battlefield of yelling soldiers and spilled blood. Amid the clamor, he sees NICK rushing forward.

NICK
(panicked)
Nick! Nick! Thank God you’re here! I thought I was going to die.

Action: In the dream, NICK’s face twists in anger. Suddenly, a long knife flashes. NICK’s hand thrusts it into NARRATOR’s chest.

NARRATOR
(shocked, whispering)
Nick... why?

Action: The dream shatters as NARRATOR wakes with a gasp. His heart pounds fiercely. The sterile room returns, the memory of betrayal lingering like a cold shadow.

  
INT. KIRK STREET APARTMENT - NIGHT

Action: Later that night, back at the apartment, NARRATOR tucks MA into bed. He explains the plastic pill organizer—a bright blue container marked with each day. MA watches with a mix of confusion and subdued amusement.

MA
(softly)
Well, that looks a little overwhelming.

NARRATOR
(gently)
Don’t worry, Ma. I’m here to help you keep it all straight.

Action: Their quiet moment is interrupted by the front door swinging open. NICK strides in, his face red and features contorted with irritation.

NICK
(laughing harshly)
What’s up, little bro? You got Ma all tucked in? Man, you should’ve been a nurse!

NARRATOR
(accusingly)
Knock it off, Nick. Somebody has to keep Ma on track. Where have you been?

NICK
(defiant)
Don’t start giving ME shit. I was at work—more than you can say for your sorry ass down at that pizza place.

Action: Tension mounts as NARRATOR’s anger flares. His fists clench. NICK, unable to hold back, slaps NARRATOR across the head. The room falls silent.

NARRATOR
(voice shaking)
Don’t you EVER talk about my mother like that, you little fuck!

Action: NICK storms out, slamming the door. NARRATOR, bruised and bitter, stares at the medication container as conflicting emotions churn inside him.

  
INT. KIRK STREET APARTMENT - LATE NIGHT

Action: The apartment is dark and heavy with aftermath. NARRATOR sits at a cluttered kitchen table, his head swollen and bruised. A single lamp casts long shadows across the room. He rubs his temple as the tension of earlier violence lingers.

Action: A soft knock at the door interrupts his isolation. DR. CARSON enters, concern etched on his face.

DR. CARSON
(in a quiet, measured tone)
I heard a commotion. What happened?

NARRATOR
(voice low and pained)
I… lost control. Nick was here... and I... I don’t know who I’m becoming.

DR. CARSON
(firmly, yet compassionately)
Violence only deepens the wounds, both seen and hidden. We must heal before this breaks us apart completely.

Action: A creak from upstairs signals another presence. MA’s distant, gentle call echoes from the dim corridor.

MA (O.S.)
(calling softly)
If anyone needs me, I’m here…

Action: DR. CARSON and NARRATOR share a heavy glance. The silence swells with regret and resolve.

DR. CARSON
(sincere)
For now, try to let the anger subside. Rest, and we’ll figure out the next step.

Action: NARRATOR’s hand trembles as he sets it on the table.

  
EXT. KIRK STREET APARTMENT - NIGHT

Action: Under a flickering streetlight, NICK paces the narrow front stoop. His face, half-hidden in shadow, is a mask of seething anger and reluctant remorse. He stops and glances at the closed apartment door.

Action: NICK pulls out his phone and dials briskly, his voice a harsh whisper.

NICK
(muttering bitterly)
I did what had to be done... but damn, what have I set in motion?

Action: The call ends abruptly. NICK’s eyes narrow as distant sirens begin to wail. He resumes his pacing, each step heavy with conflicted determination.

  
INT. SCHOOL YARD - SPRING DAY

Action: A bright school yard bathed in light. Fourth-graders laugh and trade childish insults among blooming lilac bushes.

JENNIFER BALES
(know-it-all)
You guys are in so much trouble when Mrs. Stark finds out you’re making fun of her!

Action: SUE SOMETHING-OR-OTHER shakes her head, while BOBBY SWENSON giggles. Suddenly, a tall, confident sixth-grader—NICK—strides into view.

NICK
(chiding)
What are you two numbskulls doin’?

Action: The children quiet down. BOBBY swallows nervously while a younger boy—the young NARRATOR—bursts into laughter and retorts lightly.

  
INT. NARRATOR’S BEDROOM - LATE NIGHT

Action: In a modest room lit by a soft bedside lamp, the adult NARRATOR sits on the edge of his unmade bed. NICK enters quietly, his heavy boots thudding on worn floorboards.

NICK
(calmly, yet edged)
How was your day, little bro? You okay?

Action: The NARRATOR hesitates then offers a tired smile, his eyes a mix of amusement and regret.

NARRATOR
(quietly)
It was... a day of memories and stubborn lessons. Things aren’t as simple as they seem.

Action: The brothers exchange a long, heavy glance before NICK settles into a chair, shifting between mischief and concern.

  
INT. PIZZA PARLOR - AFTERNOON

Action: In a small, worn pizza parlor, the NARRATOR stands by the front window. Outside, the world awakens to warmer weather. He gazes thoughtfully; his reflection merges with the busy street scene.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
It was a moment of solitude—thinking back to simpler times, the chaos of grade school laughter, and the promise of change. Here, plans for community college and caring for Ma mingle with memories of youthful defiance.

Action: A newspaper and scattered notes lie on a table as the NARRATOR traces a finger over them.

  
INT. NICK’S APARTMENT LIVING ROOM - NIGHT

Action: A dim living room with worn furniture and scattered mementos. NICK lounges on a couch in his brown suede jacket. BOB and SAMMY, rough-around-the-edges friends, sit nearby. The NARRATOR sits in a rocking chair.

NICK
(laughing heartily)
Man, you haven’t been to my place for ages, so listen up—tonight, we’re making some noise!

BOB
(bemused)
I swear, these girlfriends… they change you, man.

SAMMY
(smirking)
Yeah, until they don’t. One minute you’re on top of the world—next, you’re just another guy on the rocks.

Action: The NARRATOR forces a smile, his eyes betraying inner conflict.

NARRATOR
(under his breath)
Sometimes the past feels heavier than the drink in my hand.

  
INT. JOE’S BAR AND GRILL - NIGHT

Action: In a crowded bar with neon reflections dancing over pool tables, NICK strides in flanked by rowdy friends. He soon confronts LINDSEY—a pretty blonde in a pink sweater—accompanied by a protective, dark-haired MYSTERY MAN.

NICK
(agitated)
What’s up, Lindsey? Who’s that with you?

LINDSEY
(coolly)
Nick, why does it matter? He’s just someone.

Action: The MYSTERY MAN steps forward, his eyes hard and tense as murmurs ripple through the room.

MYSTERY MAN
(angry)
Who the hell are you to ask? I don’t take kindly to prying.

Action: Tension mounts. NICK’s face twists with fury, his clenched fists rising. The patrons fall silent as raised voices dominate.

NICK
(shouting)
Keep out of this—if you don’t back off, you’re gonna regret it!

Action: A head-butt and scuffle erupt as a bouncer and the bartender, JOE, rush in to intervene. Chaos reigns.

  
EXT. CITY SIDEWALK - NIGHT

Action: Under harsh streetlights, the NARRATOR bolts down a rain-slicked sidewalk. His footsteps echo as he dodges onlookers. The distant roar of the bar brawl mixes with shrill sirens.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
I ran like I’d never run before—fear and regret chasing every step. The night was no longer just noise, but a relentless heartbeat of a life unraveling.

Action: With each pounding step, his breathing grows ragged. The city blurs into streaks of neon and shadow.

  
INT. SIONNA’S APARTMENT - NIGHT

Action: In a warmly lit, modest apartment adorned with comforting touches, SIONNA waits with quiet concern. The door opens and the disheveled, trembling NARRATOR enters.

SIONNA
(gently)
You’re hurt, aren’t you? Come, sit. Tell me what happened.

Action: The NARRATOR sinks onto a worn sofa. SIONNA moves to his side, rubbing his back soothingly as he recounts the events—the anger, the violence, and a fractured bond.

NARRATOR
(voice soft, conflicted)
He lost control tonight... I’m scared, Sionna. I don’t know if I can keep up with all of this.

SIONNA
(calming)
Your strength isn’t measured by the storms you face, but by how you let them change you. You’ve come so far. Let’s just rest for now.

  
EXT. LAKE SHORE - NIGHT

Action: In a secluded stretch by a quiet lake, the NARRATOR wanders alone. The moon casts silver ripples on the water. His boots crunch softly on sandy ground as he approaches the edge.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
I needed to feel something pure—a reminder of life’s gentler pulse.

Action: He cups his hands and drinks deeply, the cool water a momentary balm. Suddenly, the wind howls and the lake’s surface trembles. From the rippling darkness, a figure emerges—a woman with long flowing brown hair and striking light blue eyes. Her white gown billows as if animated by th

  
INT. NICK'S APARTMENT - DAY

Action: In a cluttered apartment, NARRATOR offers an apology. NICK’s angry eyes flash as he processes the words. Papers tremble in the background as tension builds.

NICK
(voice low and raw)
You think a few words can fix what’s been broken?

NARRATOR
I—I never meant to make things worse. I just wanted Ma to know you’re not alone.

Action: NICK paces a short circle, his anger briefly wavering as vulnerability crosses his scarred face.

NICK
(snarling, then softer)
I’m not asking for your pity. I’m trying to figure out who I am now...without all the crap that’s piled on me.

NARRATOR
Please, Nick...Ma’s hurting, and I’m hurting too. I just want to help.

Action: For a long moment, Nick’s features twist in inner conflict. Finally, he shuffles toward the kitchen, retrieving a cold cup of coffee.

NICK
(bitterly)
Maybe I should get my shit together instead of waiting for someone to fix it. Go on—just leave.

Action: NARRATOR hesitates, then slowly rises, his face a mix of relief and sorrow.

NARRATOR
(quietly)
I understand.

  
EXT. NICK'S APARTMENT BUILDING - DAY

Action: NARRATOR exits into a bustling street. Late-day light casts long shadows on the brick facade as city noise swirls. His eyes betray deep conflict—regret, determination, and uncertainty intermingling.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
My words hung in the air like ash, neither mending nor worsening the rift. I wasn’t sure if I had done enough to ease Nick’s burden—but Ma, and even I, had no time to wallow. I had to face these hard truths head-on, however bruised my pride.

Action: He walks slowly down the sidewalk, each step heavy with responsibility and the echo of his doubts.

  
INT. MA'S APARTMENT LIVING ROOM - DAY

Action: In a modest, cluttered living room, MA sits on a well-worn couch, her eyes alight with excitement. NARRATOR stands uncertainly near a small table. NICK looms in the background, tense, while SIONNA arranges plates on a low coffee table.

NICK
Well, let me tell you something. You… YOU… are not the brother I knew, man. You’re not! All I know is now you’re some hot shit college kid with a hoity-toity girlfriend, and you know everything. Everything!

NARRATOR
Nick, I’m not like that. I’m not. You just need to come over and see Ma and me more often. If you met Sionna, I know you would like her. Yes, she is smart. Yes, I am trying to dig my way out of my stupid job. But that’s all, man. That’s all there is to it. I don’t know everything. I hardly know anything. That’s the thing about going to school—you find out how much there is out there that you don’t know.

Action: Nick’s eyes flash with anger before softening into reluctant contemplation as he sinks back onto the couch. The silence grows heavy.

NICK
I don’t really give a shit how hard you’re working. I don’t give two shits about your girlfriend, and I don’t give three shits about how dumb you are. But here’s what I have to say: You are my little brother. I do care about you and Ma, and I’ll let it slide this time. But don’t you ever, EVER interrupt me in public again. You got that?

NARRATOR
Yes, Nick. I got that. I’ve been trying to fix things since I heard that truly fucked up story—like, do they really think I could stop you? It’s just a stupid made-up story.

NICK
It is a stupid made-up story. And yes, you will stop it. And yes, you could never stop me from doing what I want in a million years.

NARRATOR
(pleading)
So, will you see Ma? She’s dyin’ to see you, man.

Action: MA’s face brightens as she leans forward.

MA
Oh, my dear, I’ve missed you so much!

NARRATOR
I’ll come over there tomorrow—just say you’re feeling unwell, alright? Don’t tell her about any of this.

NICK
(voice rising)
Of course not! You know Ma—hell, she even cried today because she forgot the burner was on. Took me half an hour to calm her down. She’s losing her memory, big-time.

MA
(smiling gently)
Yes, dear. We manage somehow.

NARRATOR
Thanks, Nick. It means a lot that you can forgive me. We’ll see you tomorrow then?

NICK
Yeah, yeah. See you tomorrow.

Action: Nick stands and heads for the door. The soft click marks his exit. Later, SIONNA places two plates of pie on the table as MA bursts into a warm laugh. NARRATOR watches, caught between hope and lingering tension.

  
INT. SIONNA’S TOYOTA CIVIC - DAY

Action: Inside an aging Toyota Civic, daylight streams over the Eastern Wisconsin hills. NARRATOR sits in the passenger seat, gaze thoughtful. SIONNA drives steadily, splitting her focus between the road and quiet reminiscence.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
I couldn’t quite wrap my head around it—Nick, that tough, stormy figure, softening enough to take Ma to mass. Was it genuine change or merely a different kind of reckoning? In that moment, responsibility and doubt warred within me.

SIONNA
(softly, with a smile)
They actually like being called Mushroom and Ginger. You’re sure about that nickname?

NARRATOR
(chuckling)
Absolutely. They’ve gone by Mushroom and Ginger since the '60s. They insist on it.

SIONNA
Remembering
They were raised right here in the Midwest, given proper names. And yet, my dad’s family was a wild mess—loud arguments, tears streaming down old faces. I can still picture my grandma in that cheap blue polyester dress, her hair piled in a beehive, watching helplessly.

NARRATOR
(awed, reflective)
That sounds… complicated.

SIONNA
(nodding)
Mom’s parents tried their best, but Grandma and Grandpa just never got the new ways—no tofu, no homemade yogurt, not even the tooth fairy or Santa Claus. It made you keep your hopes in check, never getting too carried away.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
I mused over Nick’s contradictions—a fierce warrior in one breath, a soft caretaker in the next. Life, with all its burdens and unexpected turns, was teaching us to evolve, however uncomfortably.

Action: The car eases along winding roads as the rhythmic passing of trees accompanies their quiet reflection.

  
INT. MA'S APARTMENT LIVING ROOM - DAY

Action: NARRATOR enters a quiet, dim living room. The familiar chair where MA sat now stands empty. Her purse rests on the table and a red blinking light on the telephone catches his attention. He picks it up and listens as recorded messages play.

NARRATOR
(voice trembling)
Five missed calls… and voices I don’t recognize.

Action: He rewinds the tape. A gravely recorded message from OFFICER DUPUIS urges him to come in for a word. NARRATOR’s eyes widen with dread; he grabs his bike and pedals off.

  
INT. POLICE STATION LOBBY - DAY

Action: NARRATOR steps into an ancient stone building. In the busy lobby, a brunette OFFICER DUPUIS behind a chest-high counter offers him a cup of coffee.

OFFICER DUPUIS
(calming, formal)
Mr. Olson, please have a seat. We need to discuss the accident from last night—your brother, Nick, and your mother were involved.

Action: NARRATOR clutches a styrofoam cup, his hand shaking. The officer explains that NICK is in serious condition, while MA did not survive the crash.

NARRATOR
(hoarse)
My... my mother… and Nick—what happened?

OFFICER DUPUIS
(gently)
Nick sustained multiple injuries. He’s heading into surgery soon. As for your mother, we believe she passed away on scene. We’ll assist you through the next steps.

Action: NARRATOR’s face flickers with shock as he looks down at his trembling hands. He is handed a phone to leave a brief message for SIONNA before being escorted out.

  
INT. HOSPITAL ICU - DAY

Action: Under harsh fluorescent lights, NARRATOR enters Nick’s room. NICK lies in a hospital bed, tubes and wires entangling his battered body. His wild, freckled hair stands disarrayed.

NICK
(weakly, with a strained smile)
Hey, bro.

NARRATOR
(stiffly)
Hey.

Action: For a long moment, silence prevails. Then, with uncontained fury bubbling, NARRATOR’s eyes darken.

NARRATOR
(low, bitter)
Die, you fucking jackass. Die. Die.

Action: Tears mingle with anger as NICK’s bloodshot eyes well with regret. The TV flickers in the background as NARRATOR’s heart pounds.

  
INT. FUNERAL HOME - DAY

Action: In a sparsely lit office at the funeral home, NARRATOR and SIONNA sit across from an elderly FUNERAL DIRECTOR. Papers and options for caskets and vaults lie spread before them.

FUNERAL DIRECTOR
(sincerely matter-of-fact)
We have several options—a top-line casket with engraved flowers, a pink chiffon lining, and a vault suitable for protection against the elements. How would you like it?

SIONNA
(softly, steady)
Let’s not overdo it. Ma was a practical woman. A moderately priced casket and a simple plot at the Catholic cemetery should suffice.

Action: NARRATOR nods silently, eyes distant as he remembers when life was normal.

  
EXT. CATHOLIC CEMETERY - DAY

Action: Under a pale autumn sky, NARRATOR stands before MA’s grave. A light maple-colored casket lies beneath freshly turned earth. He gently overturns an inverted metal vase and arranges a few golden mums, his tears mingling with dew.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
(quiet, reflective)
Mother: Olivia Anne Olson. You fought the good fight... you kept the faith. Now, may you finally rest in peace, free of worry and pain.

Action: The late fall sun casts long shadows as NARRATOR lingers, lost in memory and sorrow.

  
INT. PIZZA PARLOR - DAY

Action: The aroma of dough and melted cheese fills the air. NARRATOR, now working behind the counter, expertly prepares pizzas. TONY, the owner, hands him a set of car keys with a nod.

TONY
(casual, caring)
You’re fast, kid. How would you like to run some deliveries? It’s good to get out for a while.

Action: BOB—NICK’s friend—suddenly appears, eyes wide with worry.

BOB
(agitated)
Man, what’s going on with Nick? I heard the cops are after him now. This accident… it’s getting out of hand!

NARRATOR
(bitterly, with a forced chuckle)
He’s supposed to have just killed our Ma, isn’t he? I don’t even know what to say anymore.

Action: Bob backs off as the phone rings, slicing through the parlor’s murmur. NARRATOR listens, his gaze darkening with silent, unresolved anger.

  
INT. SIONNA’S APARTMENT LIVING ROOM - NIGHT

Action: In a modest, quiet living room, NARRATOR returns home. Exhaustion etches his face. He plants a tender kiss on SIONNA’s cheek before slipping under a heavy blanket.

SIONNA
(whispering, concerned)
You okay, babe? You’ve been so… distant.

NARRATOR
(ruefully)
I had the strangest dream. We were at your parents’ house—everything was normal until... until a baby was born with a pizza for a face.

Action: SIONNA chuckles softly, shaking her head as she strokes his arm.

SIONNA
(playfully)
Sounds like you’re working too hard. Maybe it’s your mind giving birth to a new idea—something wild and unexpected, just like that.

Action: NARRATOR smiles wanly, turning away to face sleep as SIONNA’s soft presence lingers.

  
INT. COURTROOM - DAY

Action: NICK sits in a sparse courtroom wearing a black pinstriped suit. His palms sweat as a heavy silence fills the room. A portly JUDGE with large glasses addresses him.

JUDGE
Mr. Olson, you stand charged with involuntary manslaughter—your actions while intoxicated have left us no choice. A jury of your peers will decide your fate.

NICK
(bitterly)
I never meant for any of this... I was just trying to fix things.

Action: Murmurs swell as NICK’s eyes burn with anger and despair. A court official ushers him into a small adjoining room.

  
INT. COURTROOM HALLWAY - CONTINUOUS

Action: In a cramped waiting room adjacent to the courtroom, DANIEL DAWSON, a sharp-tongued lawyer in a worn suit with neatly combed blond hair, sits across from NICK. Papers and a battered briefcase lie on the table.

DANIEL DAWSON
(low, measured)
Listen, Nick. They’re talking ten years if they charge you with vehicular manslaughter—even if it’s downgraded, jail isn’t far off.

NICK
(disgusted)
I can’t work. I can’t drive. I’m drowning here, and it’s all because of one mistake and one meddling... one bitch.

DANIEL DAWSON
(somber)
You’re being judged by strangers now, Nick. There’s no easy way out.

Action: NICK clenches his fists, his bitter glare meeting DANIEL DAWSON’s steady eyes.

  
EXT. CITY STREET - NIGHT

Action: Under a gloomy, rain-laden sky, NICK trudges along an empty street. Puddles reflect the harsh glare of neon signs. A solitary cigarette dangles from his lips, its smoke mingling with the cold mist.

NICK (V.O.)
I walk these cracked streets in a night that sucks every bit of warmth out of me. Bills to pay, a broken future—no cure for this bitter chill.

Action: He pulls his coat tighter and continues, shoulders tensed with unresolved rage.

  
EXT. CITY BUS STOP - NIGHT

Action: NICK arrives at a decrepit bus stop. Ragged figures huddle in the cold. The aging bus driver gives NICK a wary glance as he steps into the shelter.

NICK (V.O.)
Bus route number 10—my ride to nowhere. Each tired face here tells a story of defeat. I’m just another lost soul trying to escape the past.

Action: NICK fumbles to pay his fare with his left hand, his right still stained with blood. The bus doors hiss shut, swallowing him into the dark night.

  
INT. SARONA’S APARTMENT LIVING ROOM - NIGHT

Action: In a modest, dim living room decorated with faded drapes, the door creaks open. SARONA, a stoic yet anxious woman with watery blue eyes, appears.

SARONA
(softly)
Nick? Is that you? I... I never expected you here.

NICK
(voice trembling with fury)
Yeah, it’s me. And listen—you’re the one who messed with my brother. Because of you, everything’s falling apart.

Action: SARONA steps back, clutching a dish rag. Her expression shifts to concern as NICK blocks her path.

SARONA
(pleading)
Nick, please—talk to me. I don’t know what’s gotten into you.

NICK
(enraged)
If it weren’t for you stringing my brother along with your crazy ideas, things would be fine. Get away from him. Now.

Action: NICK roughly grabs SARONA by the arm and shoves her toward the wall. He slowly produces a glistening switchblade, flicking it open.

NICK (cont’d)
(icy threat)
Hear this well, you little whore: break it off with him tonight, come up with the cash, and stay out of my brother’s life. One wrong move, and this blade won’t wait.

Action: SARONA’s eyes widen in terror as she struggles against NICK’s grip. Suddenly, a heavy thunk is heard as the front door slams. NICK mutters:

NICK (cont’d)
(muttering)
That little shit...

Action: In that moment, NICK’s brother intervenes, seizing his arm. Amid the struggle, NICK shoves his elbow into his brother’s head, his grip loosening. The knife slips, slicing into SARONA’s shirt as crimson stains bloom.

SARONA
(squeaking in pain)
Nick, stop...

NICK
(gritting his teeth)
Damn it... I’ve got to get out.

Action: NICK wipes the blood from the blade on SARONA’s fabric and dashes out into the shrouded night.

  
INT. FERRY DECK - DAY

Action: The grey metallic deck of a ferry shimmers under a muted sky. Commuters stand in line for coffee and breakfast. DANIEL stands holding a warm cup of coffee and a burrito wrapped in silver foil. His eyes drift as he recalls a childhood nightmare—a moment when a small hand nearly escaped a fatal fall over a banister.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
On this deck I once clutched life itself, as a tiny hand dangled over the edge. I was both the rescuer and the lost child, teetering on a razor’s edge, every tremor a reminder of fate’s cruelty.

Action: The camera lingers on DANIEL’s haunted look.

  
INT. LOWELL’S RESTAURANT - DAY

Action: Sunlight streams through grand windows overlooking Puget Sound. DANIEL sits at a table on the second floor, a cinnamon roll before him. The sugary glaze glistens—a bittersweet halo to memories of love and loss.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Each bite of sweetness unspooled memories of hospital halls, of pale faces fighting for every breath. I was once Sionna’s savior, and yet the scars of that day never left.

Action: DANIEL’s hand trembles as he lifts the cinnamon roll.

  
INT. YOGA STUDIO - EVENING

Action: Dim candlelight dances across a quiet, incense-laden room. A small group sits on mats in a circle. DANIEL, in reflective silence, follows the instructor’s measured movements.

INSTRUCTOR
(softly, leading the chant)
Grateful... for each breath, for each moment of release.

Action: DANIEL’s closed eyes and relaxed face reveal a stirring transformation as the mantra washes over him.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
In that sacred space of silence and flickering light, I learned to let go – to trade bitterness for the soft weight of forgiveness.

  
EXT. OLD APARTMENT PORCH - DAY

Action: A familiar, weathered brick building stands under a cool sky. DANIEL pulls up in his car beside a modest, timeworn porch. He steps out and gently touches the door, closing his eyes as memories of laughter and shared dreams drift back.

DANIEL
(whispering softly)
There was a time when this porch was home… full of hope and shared dreams.

Action: A heavy sigh escapes him as he turns away, the past acknowledged and set aside.

  
INT. PRISON VISITATION ROOM - DAY

Action: In a sterile visitation room guarded by burly officers, DANIEL sits at a bolted table. Moments later, NICK is led in—a gaunt figure with graying hair and sorrow etched on every line.

DANIEL
(steadily)
Hi, Nick. Good to see you finally. How are you holding up?

NICK
(voice gravelly, resigned)
It’s not a cakewalk, but I’m managing... running on routine and regret.

Action: Silence deepens as DANIEL gathers himself. His eyes harden with resolve, pain intermingling with calm.

DANIEL
(quietly, but firmly)
Listen, Nick—I’ve spent years carrying the weight of your choices. The guilt for Ma, the loss of Sionna… all these years made me your captive. But today, I say this: I forgive you. I forgive you not to excuse your actions, but to free myself. I’m done living under your shadow... and under my own grief.

Action: NICK’s eyes fill with tears as his voice trembles.

NICK
(softly)
I… I’m so sorry, man. I never thought… I never meant to hurt you.

Action: A guard steps forward as minutes tick by.

GUARD
Time’s almost up, Mr. Olson.

Action: DANIEL swallows hard, nods, and leans forward.

DANIEL
I still love you, Nick. I hope one day you find the strength to change.

Action: NICK bows his head as tears fall. The guard ushers him away, leaving DANIEL alone with the ringing silence of the receiver.

  
INT. AIRPORT BOARDING AREA - DAY

Action: In a bustling terminal awash with hurried travelers and soft announcements, DANIEL sits quietly in the boarding area. He clutches a small bag of mixed nuts and an iced tea. His eyes wander over the room, serene and unburdened.

Action: He glances down at his boarding pass; a wry smile plays on his lips as he reads the name printed beneath it.

DANIEL
(softly, to himself)
President Olson. That’s me.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
And in that moment, the weight of thirty years lifted—a final chapter closed, a future reborn without chains.

Action: DANIEL closes his eyes momentarily, savoring the freedom of his new beginning.

  
FADE OUT.

THE END
